# Opengrep / Semgrep exclude list for nr-mcp-agent.
#
# Consumed by the `security / SAST (Opengrep)` CI job (typo3-ci-workflows
# security.yml). Opengrep scans production source; build artefacts, vendored
# code and test fixtures are excluded to avoid false-positive findings.

# Build artefacts and vendored code.
.Build/
.ddev/
.idea/
.vscode/
node_modules/
vendor/

# Vendored third-party frontend libraries (e.g. the bundled marked.js parser) —
# upstream code, not ours to scan (avoids false positives such as
# detect-non-literal-regexp inside the library).
Resources/Public/JavaScript/Vendor/

# Test code is covered by our own test suites + PHPStan; opengrep's default
# ruleset flags legitimate test patterns such as unlink() for fixture cleanup,
# which is safe on static test paths.
Tests/

# Build / tooling scripts are reviewed manually and not shipped.
Build/Scripts/
Build/scripts/

# Documentation renders shouldn't be scanned as source.
Documentation-GENERATED-temp/
